    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": " \n                          VETO MESSAGE - No. 92\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 5983-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\n      prohibiting the application of pesticides to certain local  fresh-\n      water wetlands\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would allow a local government that has implemented a fresh-\nwater  wetlands  protection law or ordinance in accordance with Environ-\nmental Conservation Law Section 24-0501 to adopt a local  law  or  ordi-\nnance   to  prohibit  the  application  of  pesticides  to  wetlands  it\nregulates.\n \n  This bill is similar to legislation I vetoed last year due to concerns\nthat it would undermine the integrity of the Department of Environmental\nConservation's pesticide program, which is based on extensive scientific\nreview. Additionally, this bill as written would  create  confusion  and\ncould  result in the inconsistent application of state law and inadvert-\nent consequences for pesticide regulation in New York.\n \n  Therefore, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
    "vetoNumber": 92,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2025
   }
